      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi, Thank you for reviewing. Perhaps you saw I created ticket 622 for WebP. So I had added some compile time static analysis to identify this issue (bounds checking). The optimizer couldn\u0027t be sure that the idx into sorted[] array was always within the bounds. offset[symbol_code_length] is generated on line 111, and the optimizer can\u0027t be sure it is a safe index to use.\n\nFrom line 256 BuildHuffmanTable is called with a sorted that may be SORTED_SIZE_CUTOFF large, that would be larger than code_lengths_size. Otherwise line 260 does heap allocation of code_lengths_size for sorted. (Sorted is an array of uint16_t)\n\nTherefore, feels safer to add the check, the compiler doesn\u0027t optimize it out, so appears really needed.  However, even if it isn\u0027t, I doubt this branch \u0027cost\u0027 is ever perceivable by a user. Better to be 100% safe?",
      "parentUuid": "4a41a7b8_a6528780",
      "revId": "0b56dedc98cb0367a2c375651ff7820a16bee9cc",
